  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the series:\n$1+\\frac{1}{1+2}+\\frac{1}{1+2+3}+\\ldots \\ldots$. upto 10 terms, is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{18}{11}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{22}{13}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{20}{11}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{16}{9}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{T}_r=\\frac{1}{1+2+3+\\ldots+r}=\\frac{2}{r(r+1)}$\n$\\mathrm{S}_{10}=2 \\sum_{r=1}^{10} \\frac{1}{r(r+1)}=2 \\sum_{r=1}^{10}\\left[\\frac{r+1}{r(r+1)}-\\frac{r}{r(r+1)}\\right]$\n$=2 \\sum_{r=1}^{10}\\left(\\frac{1}{r}-\\frac{1}{r+1}\\right)$\n$=2\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)+\\ldots+\\left(\\frac{1}{10}-\\frac{1}{11}\\right)\\right]$\n$=2\\left[1-\\frac{1}{11}\\right]=2 \\times \\frac{10}{11}=\\frac{20}{11}$"
  }
}